text: >-
  STATE OF UTAH,

  Plaintiff,

  V.

  STIPULATED MOTION REGARDING

  ORDER TO PRESERVE EVIDENCE

  Case No. 251403576

  Judge Tony F. Graf, Jr.

  TYLER JAMES ROBINSON,

  Defendant.

  The parties hereby jointly move the Court to: (1) set aside its prematurely
  entered

  October 20, 2025, order entitled "Order Granting Motion to Preserve Evidence"
  (Dkt. #107); and

  (2) enter in its place the parties' Stipulated Order to Preserve Evidence
  attached as Exhibit 1 to

  this stipulated motion.

  FACTS

  1. On October 8, 2025, Defendant filed a Motion to Preserve Evidence. See Dkt.
  #75.

  2. Twelve days later, on October 20, 2025, and before the State's deadline to
  respond had

  expired, the Court entered an order entitled "Order Granting Motion to
  Preserve Evidence." See

  Dkt. #107.

  3. No party filed a request to submit the motion for decision.

  4. On October 22, 2025, the State filed a Response to Defendant's Motion to
  Preserve

  Evidence (Dkt. #117), and a Motion to Set Aside the October 20, 2025, Order
  Granting Motion

  to Preserve Evidence (Dkt. #116).

  5. The parties have since engaged in discussions regarding these issues and
  reached an

  agreement on the wording of an order requiring the preservation of evidence. A
  copy of that

  proposed stipulated order is attached as Exhibit 1, and filed simultaneously
  with this stipulated

  motion. See Utah R. Civ. P. 7(j)(6)(A) (requiring a proposed order to
  accompany a stipulated

  motion).

  STIPULATED MOTION

  As evidenced by their signatures below, the parties have agreed on the wording
  of an

  order to preserve evidence. See Exhibit 1. The parties therefore jointly move
  the Court to enter

  the attached stipulated order: (1) setting aside the Court's prematurely
  entered October 20, 2025,

  order; and (2) governing the preservation of evidence going forward.

  The parties agree that entering the attached stipulated order will resolve
  Defendant's

  Motion to Preserve Evidence (Dkt. #75), and the State's Motion to Set Aside
  the October 20,

  2025, Order (Dkt. #116).
